Headers <pre><code>fatoora_ffi.h
fatoora.h
</code></pre> <p>Returns</p> <ul> <li><code>fatoora_ffi.h</code>: full ABI surface.</li> <li><code>fatoora.h</code>: alias header without the fatoora_ prefix (compile with -DFATOORA_FFI_NO_PREFIX).</li> </ul> Ownership and results <ul> <li>Opaque handles (Ffi) are created and freed with explicit _free functions.</li> <li>All fallible calls return FfiResult. <li>Strings and byte buffers returned from FFI must be freed by the caller.</li> Result and buffers <pre><code>struct FfiResult&lt;T&gt; { bool ok; T value; FfiError* error; }
struct FfiError { int32_t code; char* message; }
struct FfiString { char* ptr; }
struct FfiBytes { uint8_t* ptr; uintptr_t len; }
struct FfiBytesList { FfiBytes* ptr; uintptr_t len; }
</code></pre> <p>Returns</p> <ul> <li><code>FfiResult&lt;T&gt;</code>: check ok before using value.</li> <li><code>FfiString</code> / <code>FfiBytes</code> / <code>FfiBytesList</code>: heap buffers that must be freed by the caller.</li> </ul> Error helpers <pre><code>enum FfiErrorKind { ... };
int fatoora_error_code(FfiError* error);
FfiString fatoora_error_message(FfiError* error);
void fatoora_error_free(FfiError* error);
</code></pre> <p>Args</p> <ul> <li><code>error</code>: error handle from a failed FFI call.</li> </ul> <p>Returns</p> <ul> <li><code>code</code>: numeric error kind.</li> <li><code>message</code>: UTF-8 error message.</li> </ul> <p>Notes</p> <ul> <li>FFI error codes map directly to Rust ErrorKind and Python FfiErrorKind.</li> <li>Some getters return optional handles (NULL pointer on success when the field is absent).</li> <li>Signed invoice getters return signature metadata (hash, signature, public key, signed props hash, signing time) as UTF-8 strings.</li> </ul>
